
<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Comprehensive Manufacturing ERP Flow Manual</title>
<style>
    body { font-family: "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; padding: 20px; }
    h1 { color: #0f172a; font-size: 26px; border-bottom: 2px solid #3b82f6; padding-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 30px; }
    h2 { color: #1e293b; font-size: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 25px; }
    h3 { color: #2563eb; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 20px; }
    p { margin-bottom: 15px; }
    ul { margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px; }
    li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
    code { font-family: "Courier New", Courier, monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; color: #0f172a; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0; font-size: 13px; }
    th { background-color: #3b82f6; color: #ffffff; text-align: left; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; }
    td { padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; vertical-align: top; }
    tr:nth-child(even) { background-color: #f8fafc; }
    .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 12px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; }
    .badge-shortage { background-color: #fee2e2; color: #dc2626; }
    .badge-ok { background-color: #dcfce7; color: #16a34a; }
    .badge-alloc { background-color: #dbeafe; color: #2563eb; }
    .highlight { background-color: #fef08a; padding: 2px 4px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 50px; border-bottom: 3px double #3b82f6; padding-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 32px; color: #1e3a8a; border: none; margin-bottom: 5px;">MANUFACTURING ERP</h1>
    <h2 style="font-size: 20px; color: #64748b; border: none; margin-top: 0;">Comprehensive End-to-End Flow Manual</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 12px; color: #94a3b8;">Generated on 16-Jun-2026 12:40</p>
</div>

<h1>1. Administration & Master Setup</h1>
<p>Before any active transactions can take place, the core master data must be established in the system to ensure correct authorization, financial rules, and catalog definitions.</p>

<h2>1.1 Users, Roles & Permissions</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Admin goes to User Management, creates employee accounts, and assigns permissions by checking the access boxes (e.g., designer, purchase head, storekeeper).</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>UserController</code>, <code>RoleController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_user</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_role</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_user_roles</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_permission</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>1.2 Approval Matrix</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Admin defines financial thresholds and department workflows for Purchase Requisitions (PR) and Purchase Orders (PO) to enforce manager sign-offs.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>ApprovalMatrixController</code></li>
            <li>Table: <code>sameepaccounting_approval_matrix</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>1.3 Inventory Item Masters</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Inventory manager defines units of measurement (e.g., Kgs, Nos, Mtr), category groupings, and catalog items (raw materials, components, services, and finished products).</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>InventoryController</code>, <code>ItemCategoryController</code>, <code>ItemGroupController</code>, <code>UnitController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_inventory</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_category</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_item_group_master</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_units</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>1.4 Customer & Supplier Masters</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Sales team registers customers; Procurement registers suppliers, including bank details, contact information, and GST numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>CustomerController</code>, <code>SupplierController</code>, <code>BankdetailController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_customer</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_supplier</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_bank_details</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h1>2. Engineering & Design</h1>

<h2>2.1 Project Setup</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Project Coordinator creates a project structure, establishing a unique project code (e.g., <code>P-2026-001</code>) linked to a specific customer.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>ProjectController</code></li>
            <li>Table: <code>sameepaccounting_project</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>2.2 Drawings & Revisions</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Design engineers upload drawings, linking them to the Project Code and Sales Order. Revision control is maintained (e.g., drawing versioning on update).</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>DrawingController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_drawing_master</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_drawing_revisions</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_drawing_files</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>2.3 Bill of Materials (BOM) & Revisioning</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Designers build BOMs listing components required to manufacture a unit of a finished product. Revisions are tracked (e.g., <code>-R0</code>, <code>-R1</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>BomController</code>, <code>BomImportController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_bom_total</code> (Header), <code>sameepaccounting_bom</code> (Lines)</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h1>3. Sales & Planning</h1>

<h2>3.1 Estimates & Quotations</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Sales team prepares quotes for customers by mapping raw materials from BOMs, applying markup rates, and printing quotation sheets.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>EstimateController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_quotation_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_quotation</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>3.2 Sales Order / Order Confirmation (OC)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Once the client accepts the quote, a Sales Order is created, locking in quantities and delivery dates, linked to the Project Code.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>SalesOrderController</code>, <code>OrderConfirmationController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_salesorder_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_salesorder</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h1>4. Production Planning & MRP</h1>

<h2>4.1 Production Planning / Scheduler</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Planning officer schedules the assembly lines, prioritizing Sales Orders and generating completion dates.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>PlanningController</code></li>
            <li>Table: <code>sameepaccounting_joborder_total</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>4.2 Material Requirements Planning (MRP Run)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Storekeeper runs MRP against the Sales Order. The system calculates requirements dynamically:
        <br><code>Gross Required = BOM Item Quantity * SO Product Quantity</code>
        <br>It evaluates this against <code>available_stock</code> (open stock) in the inventory table.
        <ul>
            <li>🔴 <span class="badge badge-shortage">Shortage</span>: Flagged for purchasing (requires PR).</li>
            <li>🟢 <span class="badge badge-ok">Stock OK</span>: Flagged for allocation (ready for reserve).</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>MaterialIssueController</code></li>
            <li>Model: <code>Material_issue_model->get_sales_order_mrp_data()</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h1>5. Procurement Lifecycle (For Shortage Replenishment)</h1>

<h2>5.1 Purchase Requisition (PR)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Store manager selects shortages on the MRP Details page and clicks <strong>Generate PR</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>RequisitionController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_purchase_requisition</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_purchase_requisition_items</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>5.2 Request for Quotation (RFQ)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Purchasing head bundles PR items, matches candidate suppliers, and creates an RFQ.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>RFQController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_rfq</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_rfq_items</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_rfq_vendor</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>5.3 Vendor Quotations & Comparative Analysis</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Suppliers send quotations. Purchase department enters the rates and generates a Comparative Statement.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>SupplierController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_vendor_quotations</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_vendor_quotation_items</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>5.4 Purchase Order (PO) & PO Amendments</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Award the PO to the selected vendor. If contract terms change, create a PO Amendment.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>PoamendmentController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_po_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_purchase_order</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_po_amendments</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>5.5 Goods Receipt Note (GRN) & Quality Control (QC)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Warehouse receives the goods. Quality inspector accepts/rejects pieces based on inspection logs.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>GrnController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_grn_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_grn</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_grn_inspection</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_grn_inspection_log</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>5.6 Inventory Inwarding & Stock Ledger</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong> Approved GRN quantities increase <code>stock</code> and <code>available_stock</code> in the inventory table, and log a <code>RECEIPT</code> in the ledger.
        <ul>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_inventory</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_stock_ledger</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h1>6. Manufacturing & Work Order Execution</h1>

<h2>6.1 Job Order (JO)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> Production head releases Job Orders to authorize assembly.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controller: <code>JobOrderController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_joborder_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_joborder</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>6.2 Material Allocation (Step 1 - Reservation)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> The storekeeper clicks <strong>Allocate</strong> on the MRP run page.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Inserts a record in <code>sameepaccounting_stock_allocations</code> (status: <code>allocated</code>).</li>
            <li>Updates inventory table: <code>allocated_stock = allocated_stock + qty</code> and <code>available_stock = stock - allocated_stock</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>No physical stock deduction happens.</strong></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>6.3 Material Issue Slip (Step 2 - MIS Stock Deduction)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Flow:</strong> When materials are released to production, the storekeeper creates a Material Issue Slip.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>MaterialIssueController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_material_issue_slips</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_material_issue_items</code></li>
            <li>Logic: Converts matching <code>stock_allocations</code> status to <code>completed</code>, decrements physical <code>stock</code> and <code>allocated_stock</code> by the quantity, and logs an <code>ISSUE</code> in the stock ledger.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h1>7. Dispatch & Invoicing</h1>

<h2>7.1 Packing List & Delivery Challan (DC)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Guide:</strong> Pack finished goods, log details in Packing List, and generate a Delivery Challan for shipment.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>DeliveryChallanController</code>, <code>ReturnableChallanController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_delivery_challan_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_delivery_challan</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>7.2 Proforma & Commercial Invoice (GST)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Guide:</strong> Invoice the customer, apply CGST/SGST/IGST, and print the commercial invoice.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>ProformaInvoiceController</code>, <code>InvoiceController</code>, <code>GstController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_invoice_total</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_invoice</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_gst_classes</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>7.3 Payments, Receipts & Ledgers</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>User Guide:</strong> Record invoice payments received and match them to the project ledger.</li>
    <li><strong>System Logic:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Controllers: <code>PaymentController</code>, <code>AdvanceController</code>, <code>CreditnoteController</code></li>
            <li>Tables: <code>sameepaccounting_payment_in</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_payment_out</code>, <code>sameepaccounting_bank_transaction</code></li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>
